  "description": "CR 701.27a transforming twice returns the permanent to its front face",
  "note": "CR 701.27a's \"its other face\" over CR 712.1's two faces: a second transform turns the permanent back, every characteristic with it. The Haskell test applied an effect transforming every creature straight to Thraben Gargoyle, which no card in the pool can turn back by play; Daybreak Ranger turns itself over and back by its own upkeep triggers instead: no spell on alice's turn 1 turns it at bob's upkeep, and alice's two Giant Growths on bob's turn turn it back at hers. Each face is read whole: name, power and toughness, subtypes, and whether the front face's {T} ability is offered (bob's flyer gives it a legal target; Nightfall Predator's {R} fight is unpayable here, so the back face offers nothing).",
